  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "Security update for ruby2.5",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "Summary"
    },
    {
      "Text": "This update for ruby2.5 fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-132825: Heap buffer overflow in case conversion of strings (bsc#1290919).\n- Double free in regular expression compilation (bsc#1290920).\n- Heap buffer overflow in Regexp#to_s (bsc#1290925).\n- Heap buffer overflow in regular expression compilation (bsc#1290924).\n- Integer overflow in case conversion of strings (bsc#1290921).\n- Out-of-bounds read in case-insensitive backreference matching (bsc#1290926).\n- Out-of-bounds read in case-insensitive regular expression matching (bsc#1290923).\n",
      "Title": "Details",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
